---
/*
  SiteSearch — the public ⌕: one field over everything a reader can reach.

  Writing, quotes, constellations, sets, songs, subjects and voices. ⚠ Not works
  — `?work=` was never implemented on the public feed, so a works row would have
  nowhere to send anybody; `search-public.ts` says so at length.

  ── WHERE IT SITS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Two triggers, one sheet, and neither placement was free.

  ⚠ DESKTOP: FIRST IN THE `.site-util` GROUP, ahead of Source. Measured before
  it was chosen — at 768px, the tightest width where the nav is still inline, a
  glyph here costs +32px where a fifth nav WORD ("Search") cost +73px; and the
  word would also have claimed that searching is a ROOM, since a nav row lists
  places and an item that opens an overlay is the one entry in the row that lies
  about what it is.

  ⚠ THE GROUP HOLDS TWO, AND IT BRIEFLY HELD THREE. Source, ⌕ and the theme
  toggle together read as a toolbar rather than as the end of a running head —
  Michael, 2026-09-15: *"not liking the three icons. seems too busy."* Part of it
  was count and part was WEIGHT: GitHub is a filled brand mark where the other
  two are hairline strokes, so they never looked like a set. The theme toggle
  moved to the footer under a rule worth keeping — **a per-visit control belongs
  in the head; a per-device control belongs in the foot** — and ⌕ went FIRST,
  because search is the one of the two a reader came for.

  ⚠ PHONE: BESIDE THE HAMBURGER, NOT INSIDE IT. The same ruling the Observatory
  took, for the same reason — a phone has no ⌘K and the menu is shut, so search
  behind it is a tap behind a door. At 390px the bar is `wordmark 158 + free 162
  + burger 30`, so this spends 30 of 162.

  ⚠ NOT BOTTOM-RIGHT, which is what the Observatory does. `SiteLayout`'s
  `backToTop` prop exists because *"constellation pages bring their own floating
  control (the sky-return ✦) — one quiet corner control at a time"*. A floating
  ⌕ would be the third thing fighting for that corner.

  ── THE SURFACE, AND THE ONE THING IT GIVES UP ─────────────────────────────

  A `.drawer-dialog`, the same right-hand sheet the Reader uses — `app.css`
  imports `admin.css`, so the class and all of its motion (slide in, `[data-
  closing]` out, backdrop fade, reduced-motion, and the `--kb` software-keyboard
  inset) are already on every public page.

  ⚠ THE SHEET NEEDS JAVASCRIPT, AND THE TRIGGER IS AN `<a>` BECAUSE OF IT. The
  public side does not assume JS the way the Observatory does — `/blog`'s rail is
  a real `<form method="get">` precisely so that search survives without it. So
  this trigger is a LINK to `/blog`, which the script upgrades into "open the
  sheet". A reader without JavaScript follows it and lands on the field that
  already works; a reader with it never leaves the page. Nothing is lost and
  nothing lies about where it goes.
*/
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import SiteSearchVerse from './SiteSearchVerse.astro';
import '../styles/site-search.css';

interface Props {
  /**
   * `util` — the desktop trigger, inside the nav's trailing icon group.
   * `bar`  — the phone trigger, beside the hamburger.
   * `sheet` — the surface, mounted once at the end of the body.
   */
  part: 'util' | 'bar' | 'sheet';
}
const { part } = Astro.props;

/* The no-JS destination, shared by both triggers — see the header. `#blog-filters`
   is the rail form's own id, so the fallback lands ON the field rather than at
   the top of a feed. */
const FALLBACK = '/blog#blog-filters';
---

{
  part === 'util' && (
    <a
      href={FALLBACK}
      data-site-search
      class="site-util rounded-field text-whisper hover:bg-base-200 hover:text-base-content inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 px-2 py-2.5 transition-colors md:justify-center md:gap-0 md:p-1.5"
      aria-label="Search"
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
    >
      <Icon name="ph:magnifying-glass" class="size-4 shrink-0" />
      {/* Inside the mobile dropdown this gets a word, exactly as Source and
          Theme do; above 768px the glyph stands alone. */}
      <span class="font-serif text-base tracking-[0.09em] [font-variant:all-small-caps] md:hidden">Search</span>
    </a>
  )
}

{
  part === 'bar' && (
    /* ⚠ `md:hidden` — the phone's own trigger. Above 768px the util above is
       visible in the inline nav and this would be a second one. */
    <a
      href={FALLBACK}
      data-site-search
      class="rounded-field text-faint hover:bg-base-200 hover:text-base-content p-1.5 md:hidden"
      aria-label="Search"
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
    >
      <Icon name="ph:magnifying-glass" class="text-lg" />
    </a>
  )
}

{
  part === 'sheet' && (
    <dialog id="site-search" class="drawer-dialog ss-sheet" aria-label="Search">
      <div class="ss-shell">
        <label class="ss-field">
          <span class="ss-mag" aria-hidden="true">
            ⌕
          </span>
          <input
            type="search"
            data-ss-input
            autocomplete="off"
            placeholder="Search everything…"
            aria-label="Search everything"
            aria-controls="ss-results"
          />
          {/* ⚠ `data-close` is the building's exit hook — `wireSheetDismiss`
              finds the ✕ by it, so this needs no listener of its own and cannot
              drift out of step with Escape and the backdrop. */}
          <button type="button" data-close class="ss-x" aria-label="Close">
            <Icon name="ph:x" class="text-lg" />
          </button>
        </label>
        <div id="ss-results" class="ss-body" data-ss-results aria-live="polite">
          <SiteSearchVerse />
        </div>
      </div>
    </dialog>
  )
}
